          "system_name": "SUSE CVE Page",
          "text": "https://www.suse.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-114642"
        }
      ],
      "notes": [
        {
          "category": "general",
          "text": "Traefik 2.11.0 before 2.11.58 and 3.0.0 before 3.7.14 stores its NTLM/Kerberos backend round tripper in a client-connection slot not keyed by ServersTransport, so one service's TLS client configuration is reused for another service's backend. An unauthenticated client can arm the slot via a backend issuing an NTLM or Negotiate challenge, then reach another service on the same keep-alive connection, bypassing its root CAs, server name, and certificate verification.",
          "title": "CVE description"
        }
      ],
